msgid "Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/27-component_servo.rst:106
msgid "Here, the ``Servo`` library is included which allows for easy control of the servo motor. The pin connected to the servo and the initial angle of the servo are also defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/27-component_servo.rst:115
msgid "The ``setup()`` function runs once when the Arduino starts. The servo is attached to the defined pin using the ``attach()`` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/27-component_servo.rst:123
msgid "The main loop has two ``for`` loops. The first loop increases the angle from 0 to 180 degrees, and the second loop decreases the angle from 180 to 0 degrees. The ``servo.write(angle)`` command sets the servo to the specified angle. The ``delay(15)`` causes the servo to wait for 15 milliseconds before moving to the next angle, controlling the speed of the scanning movement."
msgstr ""

